INSERT INTO company_dossiers (ticker,status,description,lede,sells,revenue_model,opportunity,must_go_right,editor_note,bull_title,bull_json,bear_title,bear_json,thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json,risks_json,monitor_json,questions_json,competitors,evidence_date,validated_at,published_at,updated_at) VALUES ('TSCO','published','TRACTOR SUPPLY operates in consumer discretionary, focused on rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion.','TRACTOR SUPPLY gives owners exposure to rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion. The central question is whether its competitive position and reinvestment can convert demand into durable per-share cash generation after the full cost of capital, execution, and industry risk.','TRACTOR SUPPLY provides rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion to consumers, travelers, households, merchants, franchisees, dealers, and business partners. Owners should verify segment mix, customer concentration, contract terms, and geographic exposure in the latest Form 10-K and 10-Q.','Product, service, booking, advertising, subscription, financing, franchise, and transaction revenue tied to consumer demand and brand or platform engagement.','Brand relevance, digital distribution, loyalty, network scale, premium experiences, and international expansion can grow share and lifetime value. For TRACTOR SUPPLY, the owner must test whether rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion can gain profitable share rather than treating addressable-market growth as company value by itself.','Traffic and retention must remain healthy, customer acquisition and service costs must stay rational, inventory or capacity must be productive, and capital allocation must protect per-share value.','This owner brief uses the issuer''s SEC filing history, earnings-related 8-K record, proxy disclosures, and official company materials as its evidence spine. Bull and bear points are hypotheses to verify against the latest reported segment, cash-flow, balance-sheet, and management-commentary evidence—not recommendations or price targets.','What the filing and call evidence could support','["TRACTOR SUPPLY''s position in rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume.","Brand, assortment, network effects, locations, data, distribution, and customer experience can support repeat use and pricing.","Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together.","Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion."]','What owners must be prepared to disprove','["Demand for rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow.","Recession, fashion, value perception, or weaker experiences can reduce traffic and price.","Low switching costs, promotion, or disintermediation can pressure margins.","Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash."]','The owner thesis breaks if TRACTOR SUPPLY cannot defend its position in rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion and repeatedly fails to convert reported growth into resilient per-share free cash flow after required investment, balance-sheet obligations, and dilution.','[{"label":"DEMAND & ENGAGEMENT","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"traffic, bookings, units, users, frequency, price, and mix"},{"label":"UNIT ECONOMICS","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"gross margin, acquisition cost, service cost, inventory, capacity, and retention"},{"label":"CASH & CAPITAL","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"working capital, capex, financing, leases, repurchases, and free cash flow"},{"label":"REVENUE QUALITY","value":"Growth versus durability","detail":"Separate price, volume, mix, acquisitions, foreign exchange, backlog, and one-time items; reconcile growth with retention and cash collection."},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Resilience and optionality","detail":"Track cash, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, covenants, refinancing needs, and contingent liabilities disclosed in the latest filing."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner cash conversion","detail":"Reconcile net income with operating cash, capex, acquisitions, dividends, repurchases, stock compensation, and diluted share count."}]','[{"title":"Consumer and brand demand","level":"High","text":"Recession, fashion, value perception, or weaker experiences can reduce traffic and price.","signal":"Transactions, bookings, cancellations, markdowns, and satisfaction"},{"title":"Competition and platform economics","level":"High","text":"Low switching costs, promotion, or disintermediation can pressure margins.","signal":"Market share, acquisition cost, incentives, take rate, and retention"},{"title":"Inventory, capacity, and financing","level":"High","text":"Long-lived assets, inventory, leases, or credit can amplify a demand miss.","signal":"Turns, utilization, residual values, losses, and fixed obligations"},{"title":"Capital allocation","level":"Medium","text":"Acquisitions, internal investment, debt, dividends, and repurchases can create or destroy per-share value.","signal":"Return on invested capital, impairments, leverage, share count, and post-investment cash generation"},{"title":"Reporting, legal, and governance","level":"Medium","text":"Controls, estimates, litigation, tax, incentives, or governance choices can alter reported economics and owner outcomes.","signal":"Restatements, control weaknesses, estimate changes, proceedings, proxy incentives, and related-party disclosures"}]','[{"title":"Latest 10-Q versus prior expectations","text":"Compare reported operating drivers, cash conversion, balance-sheet changes, and risk language with the prior quarter and owner thesis.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Management commentary versus delivery","text":"Record the measurable commitments made in the latest official earnings materials and test them against subsequent filings.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Downside leading indicators","text":"Watch Transactions, bookings, cancellations, markdowns, and satisfaction; Market share, acquisition cost, incentives, take rate, and retention; Turns, utilization, residual values, losses, and fixed obligations.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital allocation","text":"Measure whether retained cash, acquisitions, debt reduction, dividends, and repurchases improve durable value per diluted share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["Which disclosed operating metric best proves that TRACTOR SUPPLY is strengthening its position in rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion?","What changed in the latest 10-Q relative to the preceding 10-K and management''s prior commentary?","Which portion of reported growth is recurring, contractual, or repeatable, and which portion is cyclical or one-time?","What balance-sheet or off-balance-sheet obligation matters most in a downside case?","Does management''s compensation framework reward per-share owner value or primarily scale and adjusted metrics?","What measurable development would invalidate the thesis rather than merely create short-term price volatility?"]','TRACTOR SUPPLY competes with public and private operators across rural lifestyle retail, farm and ranch supplies, pet products, seasonal goods, loyalty, distribution, and store expansion; the comparable set below is a research starting point and must be normalized for business mix, leverage, accounting, and capital intensity.','2026-08-02',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) ON CONFLICT(ticker) DO UPDATE SET status='published',description=excluded.description,lede=excluded.lede,sells=excluded.sells,revenue_model=excluded.revenue_model,opportunity=excluded.opportunity,must_go_right=excluded.must_go_right,editor_note=excluded.editor_note,bull_title=excluded.bull_title,bull_json=excluded.bull_json,bear_title=excluded.bear_title,bear_json=excluded.bear_json,thesis_breaker=excluded.thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json=excluded.financial_drivers_json,risks_json=excluded.risks_json,monitor_json=excluded.monitor_json,questions_json=excluded.questions_json,competitors=excluded.competitors,evidence_date=excluded.evidence_date,validated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,published_at=COALESCE(company_dossiers.published_at,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
