INSERT INTO company_dossiers (ticker,status,description,lede,sells,revenue_model,opportunity,must_go_right,editor_note,bull_title,bull_json,bear_title,bear_json,thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json,risks_json,monitor_json,questions_json,competitors,evidence_date,validated_at,published_at,updated_at) VALUES ('TTD','published','TRADE DESK INC CLASS A operates in communication, focused on independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue.','TRADE DESK INC CLASS A gives owners exposure to independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue. The central question is whether its competitive position and reinvestment can convert demand into durable per-share cash generation after the full cost of capital, execution, and industry risk.','TRADE DESK INC CLASS A provides independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue to consumers, advertisers, distributors, enterprises, creators, and communications or entertainment partners. Owners should verify segment mix, customer concentration, contract terms, and geographic exposure in the latest Form 10-K and 10-Q.','Subscription, connectivity, advertising, licensing, theatrical, content, distribution, and transaction revenue across communications and media channels.','Scaled audiences, valuable intellectual property, broadband or platform distribution, and global direct relationships can support monetization. For TRADE DESK INC CLASS A, the owner must test whether independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue can gain profitable share rather than treating addressable-market growth as company value by itself.','Engagement and subscriber economics must hold, content and network investment must earn returns, debt must remain manageable, and changing distribution must not destroy legacy cash faster than new models grow.','This owner brief uses the issuer''s SEC filing history, earnings-related 8-K record, proxy disclosures, and official company materials as its evidence spine. Bull and bear points are hypotheses to verify against the latest reported segment, cash-flow, balance-sheet, and management-commentary evidence—not recommendations or price targets.','What the filing and call evidence could support','["TRADE DESK INC CLASS A''s position in independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume.","Content libraries, franchises, networks, infrastructure, data, distribution, and customer relationships can create scale and switching advantages.","Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together.","Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion."]','What owners must be prepared to disprove','["Demand for independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow.","Consumers and advertisers can shift quickly across platforms and formats.","Large commitments may not generate sufficient audience or cash returns.","Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash."]','The owner thesis breaks if TRADE DESK INC CLASS A cannot defend its position in independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue and repeatedly fails to convert reported growth into resilient per-share free cash flow after required investment, balance-sheet obligations, and dilution.','[{"label":"AUDIENCE & SUBSCRIBERS","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"users, churn, engagement, price, mix, and distribution"},{"label":"CONTENT & ADVERTISING","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"slate, rights, audience delivery, ad demand, licensing, and returns"},{"label":"CASH & CAPITAL","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"content spend, network capex, debt, restructuring, asset sales, and free cash flow"},{"label":"REVENUE QUALITY","value":"Growth versus durability","detail":"Separate price, volume, mix, acquisitions, foreign exchange, backlog, and one-time items; reconcile growth with retention and cash collection."},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Resilience and optionality","detail":"Track cash, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, covenants, refinancing needs, and contingent liabilities disclosed in the latest filing."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner cash conversion","detail":"Reconcile net income with operating cash, capex, acquisitions, dividends, repurchases, stock compensation, and diluted share count."}]','[{"title":"Audience fragmentation","level":"High","text":"Consumers and advertisers can shift quickly across platforms and formats.","signal":"Churn, engagement, ratings, ad pricing, and market share"},{"title":"Content and technology investment","level":"High","text":"Large commitments may not generate sufficient audience or cash returns.","signal":"Content amortization, slate performance, network use, and return on spend"},{"title":"Leverage and regulation","level":"High","text":"Debt, consolidation, spectrum, privacy, and distribution rules can constrain strategy.","signal":"Net leverage, refinancing, remedies, and carriage disputes"},{"title":"Capital allocation","level":"Medium","text":"Acquisitions, internal investment, debt, dividends, and repurchases can create or destroy per-share value.","signal":"Return on invested capital, impairments, leverage, share count, and post-investment cash generation"},{"title":"Reporting, legal, and governance","level":"Medium","text":"Controls, estimates, litigation, tax, incentives, or governance choices can alter reported economics and owner outcomes.","signal":"Restatements, control weaknesses, estimate changes, proceedings, proxy incentives, and related-party disclosures"}]','[{"title":"Latest 10-Q versus prior expectations","text":"Compare reported operating drivers, cash conversion, balance-sheet changes, and risk language with the prior quarter and owner thesis.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Management commentary versus delivery","text":"Record the measurable commitments made in the latest official earnings materials and test them against subsequent filings.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Downside leading indicators","text":"Watch Churn, engagement, ratings, ad pricing, and market share; Content amortization, slate performance, network use, and return on spend; Net leverage, refinancing, remedies, and carriage disputes.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital allocation","text":"Measure whether retained cash, acquisitions, debt reduction, dividends, and repurchases improve durable value per diluted share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["Which disclosed operating metric best proves that TRADE DESK INC CLASS A is strengthening its position in independent demand-side advertising platform, connected television, data, identity, measurement, and usage-based software revenue?","What changed in the latest 10-Q relative to the preceding 10-K and management''s prior commentary?","Which portion of reported growth is recurring, contractual, or repeatable, and which portion is cyclical or one-time?","What balance-sheet or off-balance-sheet obligation matters most in a downside case?","Does management''s compensation framework rewa